  "id": "DrugBank_DB09143 - MONDO_20804",
  "verbalization": "Sonidegib is implicated in the pathogenesis of Basal Cell Carcinoma (BCC) through a mechanistic pathway involving Vismodegib. The evidence suggests that Sonidegib, through its indication for Sebaceous Adenocarcinoma and Sweat Gland Cancer, leads to the activation of Vismodegib, which in turn is associated with BCC. This indicates a potential role of Vismodegib in the progression of BCC, possibly through the inhibition of certain pathways that are dysregulated in the disease. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Sonidegib influences Vismodegib and subsequently BCC remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting Vismodegib in the treatment of BCC, supported by the observed clinical and molecular links.",
